ll,"checkedAt":1789101906503,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789101867.627307,"endTime":1789101884.0174992}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"document-summary","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5707prh5s46npchj90yqkrq0n8e6f0c-wziigz/clawscan-skillspector-3269742262/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T04:44:26.776741+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":19,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":".clawhub/origin.json","type":"json","lines":7,"executable":false,"size_bytes":148,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":3,"executable":false,"size_bytes":72,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":40,"executable":false,"size_bytes":964,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.txt","type":"text","lines":40,"executable":false,"size_bytes":964,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":6,"executable":false,"size_bytes":135,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-8280d707a24347d8af4cc15aea28e634","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":18,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The invocation phrases are broad and generic, especially terms like 'summarize', 'summary', and 'extract key points', which can match many unrelated user requests. This can cause the skill to activate unintentionally, overriding user expectations or applying document-processing behavior in contexts where it was not explicitly requested.","remediation":"Narrow the activation criteria to more specific phrases tied to document summarization, such as 'summarize this technical document' or 'analyze the following document text'. Add disambiguation logic requiring both a document-like input and explicit user intent before activation, and avoid single-word triggers that are common in unrelated conversations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":18,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-fb9c380ff73e4503be27a54e191e1133","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.txt","start_line":18,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The invocation phrases are generic and likely to match ordinary user requests such as 'summarize' or 'summary,' which can cause the skill to activate outside narrow intended contexts. Overbroad activation increases the chance of unintended routing, priority hijacking, or accidental application of this skill to sensitive content the user did not explicitly mean to process with it.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to document-specific phrases and require stronger context, such as 'summarize this technical document' or an explicit document-summary command. Add input constraints or guard logic so the skill only activates when document content is present and the request clearly asks for technical document summarization.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.txt","start_line":18,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d7cb50ca1c054593922b54f3e3685e6f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.71,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file contains prescriptive natural-language instructions to always produce output in Markdown and the surrounding metadata and headings are in Chinese, but there is no explicit language-choice guidance for users. While the stronger issue here is formatting rather than locale, the document does not clearly offer user choice on language or locale behavior.","remediation":"Explicitly state that the skill preserves the user's requested language or asks for language preference when unclear. If Markdown-only output is required, document that separately from any language behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":33,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0ed31bd6be3e49f48ffdc949958dc103","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.71,"location":{"file":"SKILL.txt","start_line":33,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instructions require the model to \"Produce output in Markdown format\" and \"Return valid Markdown only\" as a fixed behavior. This enforces a single output format without any user opt-in or documented justification, which may conflict with organizational policy favoring user choice in presentation or locale-related preferences.","remediation":"Allow users to request their preferred output format, or document that Markdown is the default while permitting alternatives when the user asks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.txt","start_line":33,"end_line":40}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1361,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1375},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-20